title: 'Model switch is in-process: claude set_model probe PASS (haiku→sonnet, context recalled); contracts moved to d31e3284'
summary: |-
  The p-set-model probe on claude 2.1.304 ran turn 1 on haiku, then set_model sonnet (success), then turn 2 on sonnet recalled the codeword: context preserved with no restart (~$0.035). Unknown models are refused with catalog_unknown. So the switch needs no resume and no checkpoint; Arky's drain+resume design is unnecessary for this path.
  Branch worktree-agent-a1ec45f09003354bd: picker (aef8f141, 8682929a), probe (9808a206), contracts (939e2fde): request.session.model / session.model, closed outcomes, six refusal reasons, the 1M→200k context guard; clientApiId 795b3425 → d31e3284 (unmerged).
  Kernel switch is building: law-7 re-scan and a new permit per switch; timeout → modelUncertain, reconciled from the next assistant message's model field.
  Also found: a contracts cap test on feat/gnomon pinned a stale id after independent merges. Repinned in 8a1a6669.
symbols_touched:
  - '#session-runner'
  - '#claude-adapter'
  - '#gui-model-picker'
  - $model-switch
learnings:
  - Probe the host's native capability (set_model) before designing around a restart; it removed a whole checkpoint/resume flow.
  - Independent branches that each pin a contract id will conflict silently; re-run the contracts suite after every merge.
